```apex
public class RenewalReminderService {

    /**
     * Sends a renewal-reminder email to the owner of each given opportunity.
     *
     * All emails are batched into a single Messaging.sendEmail call (limit:
     * 10 calls / 1000 emails per transaction). Per-email failures do NOT
     * prevent other emails in the batch from being delivered; we inspect
     * the SendEmailResult[] to count actual successes.
     *
     * @param opportunityIds  up to 200 Opportunity IDs
     * @return                number of emails that were sent successfully
     */
    public static Integer sendReminders(List<Id> opportunityIds) {
        if (opportunityIds == null || opportunityIds.isEmpty()) {
            return 0;
        }

        Map<Id, Opportunity> oppMap = new Map<Id, Opportunity>(
            [SELECT Id, Name, CloseDate, OwnerId
             FROM Opportunity
             WHERE Id IN :opportunityIds]
        );

        List<Messaging.SingleEmailMessage> emails = new List<Messaging.SingleEmailMessage>();

        for (Id oppId : opportunityIds) {
            Opportunity opp = oppMap.get(oppId);
            if (opp == null || opp.OwnerId == null) {
                continue;
            }

            Messaging.SingleEmailMessage mail = new Messaging.SingleEmailMessage();
            mail.setTargetObjectId(opp.OwnerId);
            mail.setSaveAsActivity(false);
            mail.setSubject('Renewal due: ' + opp.Name);
            mail.setPlainTextBody(buildBody(opp));
            emails.add(mail);
        }

        if (emails.isEmpty()) {
            return 0;
        }

        Messaging.SendEmailResult[] results = Messaging.sendEmail(emails);

        Integer sentCount = 0;
        for (Messaging.SendEmailResult r : results) {
            if (r.isSuccess()) {
                sentCount++;
            }
        }

        return sentCount;
    }

    private static String buildBody(Opportunity opp) {
        String closeDateStr = opp.CloseDate != null
            ? opp.CloseDate.format()
            : 'an unknown date';

        return 'Hi,\n\n'
            + 'Your opportunity "' + opp.Name + '" has a close date of '
            + closeDateStr + ' and is due for renewal.\n\n'
            + 'Please review it at your earliest convenience.\n\n'
            + 'Regards';
    }
}
```

The only remaining issue is how the owner name is extracted. In the LDS wire data shape, every field is wrapped in `{ value }`, and a lookup relationship like `Owner` resolves to a nested record that has its own `fields` object. So the owner's name lives at `data.fields.Owner.value.fields.Name.value`, not `data.fields.Owner.value.Name`.

